    'cookie-policy'=>['title'=>'Cookie Policy','intro'=>'Cookies and browser storage used by GNCILink, and the choices available to you.', 'sections'=>[
        ['Your choices','Optional visitor statistics, personalization/reminders and embedded services are off until selected. Accept optional, Reject optional and Manage choices are available in the banner. Use the footer’s Privacy & cookie settings to change or withdraw your choices. We honor browser Global Privacy Control and Do Not Track signals by keeping these optional features off. Rejecting optional features does not prevent reading the public site or using the contact form.'],
        ['Essential session and preference storage','PHP’s configured session cookie (normally PHPSESSID) supports contact-form protection and staff sign-in. Server-side contact sessions can temporarily retain form entries and errors. Administrative session inactivity is limited by the configured SESSION_TIMEOUT, with a 30-minute default. The optional staff “remember this device” cookie gnc_remember_me lasts up to 30 days and is used only when requested. The gnc_privacy_v1 first-party cookie remembers your versioned category choices and choice time for 180 days. These cookies are separate from optional visitor statistics.'],
        ['Optional visitor statistics','gnc_vid is an HttpOnly first-party cookie with a random identifier and a one-year lifetime, set only when visitor statistics are enabled. The server stores its hash and visit date. The gnc_pv: browser session-storage entries limit repeated page-count requests to once per page per 30 minutes per tab. Refusing or withdrawing statistics stops new recording, clears the visitor cookie and clears these local page-count entries; it does not erase earlier stored counts or hashes.'],
        ['Optional personalization and reminders','gnc_recommendations_v1 in local storage holds your chosen personalization setting, recent page interests and reading time for up to 30 days from update; page-history entries older than 30 days are discarded on use. gnci_feedback_v1 stores invitation timing and dismissal/completion reminders, including 7-day dismissal and 30-day submission-acknowledgment cooldowns. gnci_feedback_prompt_v1 is a short cross-tab invitation lease. Withdrawing personalization clears these keys and stops the related optional timing/profile activity.'],
        ['Requested-service browser storage','gncbot.v1 in session storage retains up to 40 recent chat messages for the current tab. “New conversation” clears the displayed/stored conversation. The homepage’s gncIntroSeen session key remembers that its opening animation has played. Staff editor session-storage keys retain temporary save notices/intents. These are distinct from cross-page personalization and visitor statistics.'],
        ['Embedded services and provider storage','Google Maps, Facebook page plugins and the Google feedback form can use their own cookies or storage according to their policies and your browser settings. Embedded-services permission controls loading those supported frames; the feedback invitation additionally needs personalization. Turning permission off removes those frames, but this site cannot remove cookies belonging to another domain or recall data already sent. Use the provider’s settings and your browser controls for that. External website links remain available.'],
        ['Fonts, libraries and limitations','Pages also fetch fonts and software libraries from external delivery providers, independently of embedded-service permission. Their requests expose connection information such as IP address and browser headers. This policy does not claim to list third-party cookie names or lifetimes that were not verified in the hosted environment. Browser blocking, clearing storage or using another device may require choosing again.'],
